From: Harsh Kumar Bijlani <hbijlani@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2025 10:54:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: guard dp peer during recovery cleanup

Firmware recovery can interrupt peer setup after the link peer is added to
the datapath list but before its shared dp_peer is assigned. The recovery
cleanup already accounts for this when releasing RX TID state, but then
unconditionally dereferences the same NULL pointer while unlinking it.

Only clear the shared peer links when dp_peer is present. The link peer is
still removed from its hash and list in either case.

Adapted from Qualcomm's downstream dp_peer NULL checks.

Signed-off-by: Harsh Kumar Bijlani <hbijlani@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -1237,11 +1237,13 @@ void ath12k_mac_peer_cleanup_all(struct
 
 		/* cleanup dp peer */
 		spin_lock_bh(&dp_hw->peer_lock);
-		dp_peer = peer->dp_peer;
-		peerid_index = ath12k_dp_peer_get_peerid_index(dp, peer->peer_id);
-		rcu_assign_pointer(dp_peer->link_peers[peer->link_id], NULL);
-		rcu_assign_pointer(dp_hw->dp_peers[peerid_index], NULL);
+		if (peer->dp_peer) {
+			dp_peer = peer->dp_peer;
+			peerid_index = ath12k_dp_peer_get_peerid_index(dp, peer->peer_id);
+			rcu_assign_pointer(dp_peer->link_peers[peer->link_id], NULL);
+			rcu_assign_pointer(dp_hw->dp_peers[peerid_index], NULL);
+		}
 		spin_unlock_bh(&dp_hw->peer_lock);
 
 		ath12k_dp_link_peer_rhash_delete(dp, peer);
